--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- If you need to back out 0028
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The attachment routes go back to answering "unavailable" and a workspace
-- write naming a file is refused again (B11 Ruling W4), exactly as before.
--
-- What is lost: every household's file records, for good, because the table is
-- dropped. The objects themselves stay in the bucket until you delete them:
-- first list them with
--   select object_path from public.household_attachments
--   union select object_path from public.attachment_object_sweep;
-- and delete that folder in Storage, or the whole bucket (Storage, the bucket,
-- Empty, then Delete). Test records keep any attachments list they hold
-- (references to files that no longer exist), and ledger rows in domain
-- 'attachments' stay; they hold ids, collection names and statuses only.
--
-- The tested copy of this block is in docs/backend/YOUR_TODO.md, which is what
-- test/attachmentsSchema.test.mjs runs.
--
-- <!-- backout-0028 -->
-- drop trigger if exists operations_privacy_clear_attachments on public.operations;
-- drop trigger if exists operations_attachments_settled_guard on public.operations;
